From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov13b10: Update the exposure limit on every format change

The exposure maximum follows height + vblank and is updated from the
V4L2_CID_VBLANK handler. set_fmt sets vblank to the new mode's default,
but the control framework calls s_ctrl only when the value changes: when
vblank already had that value (for instance 76 lines set in the
2104x1560 mode before switching to 4208x3120, whose default is 76), the
exposure maximum stays at the old mode's 1560 + 76 - 8 lines, half the
frame, until streaming starts and the control handler setup runs the
VBLANK handler again. Userspace that reads the limits after set_fmt, as
libcamera does when it configures, gets the old ones. Set the limit for
the new height in set_fmt as well.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
index 41042b3b4..7f2a523e6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
@@ -1135,6 +1135,7 @@ ov13b10_set_pad_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	struct v4l2_mbus_framefmt *framefmt;
 	s32 vblank_def;
 	s32 vblank_min;
+	s64 exposure_max;
 	s64 h_blank;
 	s64 pixel_rate;
 	s64 link_freq;
@@ -1168,6 +1169,16 @@ ov13b10_set_pad_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 					 OV13B10_VTS_MAX - mode->height,
 					 1, vblank_def);
 		__v4l2_ctrl_s_ctrl(ov13b->vblank, vblank_def);
+		/*
+		 * The exposure limit follows height + vblank, but s_ctrl only
+		 * runs when vblank changes: keep the limit right for the new
+		 * height when vblank already had this value.
+		 */
+		exposure_max = mode->height + ov13b->vblank->val - 8;
+		__v4l2_ctrl_modify_range(ov13b->exposure,
+					 ov13b->exposure->minimum,
+					 exposure_max, ov13b->exposure->step,
+					 exposure_max);
 		h_blank = mode->ppl - mode->width;
 		__v4l2_ctrl_modify_range(ov13b->hblank, h_blank,
 					 h_blank, 1, h_blank);
